  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.3. Increased capacity of the ILO constituents to engage in a forward-looking international labour standards policy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2020, Tajikistan improved reporting on ratified Conventions under Article 22. The ILO organised a distance training on reporting from 26 &#x2013; 29 May 2020.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.3.1. Percentage of reports on the application of ratified Conventions due by 1 September received in a timely manner that include replies to comments of the supervisory bodies</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.2. Increased capacity of the member States to apply international labour standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In its 2020 Observation on C182, the CEACR noted with satisfaction the adoption of Government Decree No. 169 of 2014, which sets out the hazardous types of work prohibited to children under 18 years of age. The ILO supported the development of the Decree in 2013 and 2014 through the development of legislative reviews and organising tripartite discussions. Support was provided through the &quot;Elimination of child labour and human trafficking in Central Asia: commitment becomes action&quot; Project.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.2.1. Number of cases of progress in the application of ratified Conventions noted with satisfaction by the supervisory bodies</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.1. Increased capacity of the member States to ratify international labour standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tajikistan ratified P29 on 24 January 2020. The ILO supported the ratification process in 2018 and 2019 through the development of legislative reviews/support documentation and organising tripartite discussions. Support was provided through the &quot;Elimination of child labour and human trafficking in Central Asia: commitment becomes action&quot; Project.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.1.1. Number of ratifications of fundamental and governance Conventions or Protocols</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
